      "side": 1,
      "message": "`getStatusProperty()` will do async DBus calls and so if `determineResourceState()` is in `getResourceState()`, it would complete before we aggregate the Status.State properties. We could do nested callbacks to ensure that `determineResourceState()` is called only once but it would cause lots of nested callbacks if anymore properties that impact the Status.State are added. The current approach is to keep property retrieval independent and straightforward to add new properties. Let me know what you think",
